P1 - S8 - 0025 - Guard state holder (web-hook parity port of useGuard.ts)

Ported the web `useGuard` hook domain (web/src/api/hooks/useGuard.ts) to UI-free KMP shared-core
state holders at full parity. UI-free; consumed identically by Android/Apple (KMP) and Windows
(C# port via the shared golden vectors).

Production code (apps/shared/core/commonMain):
- presentation/guard/GuardModels.kt - typed wire DTOs (GuardConfig, GuardEvent, GuardEventsResponse,
  SetConfigResponse, PanicResponse, AcknowledgeResponse, SetGuardConfigInput) + the three
  golden-locked derivations: isGuardEventAcknowledged (acknowledged_at != null), guardEventsOf
  (safeArray(data?.events) unwrap), guardVehicleEnabled (enabled: vehicleId > 0 gate).
- data/repo/GuardRepository.kt - S7 port interface + guardConfigKey / guardEventsKey (the web
  guardKeys.config / guardKeys.events tuples).
- data/repo/HttpGuardRepository.kt - cache-then-network impl over ApiHttpClient; two read shapes
  cached as raw JsonElement in one CacheDomain.Guard partition, decoded per-feed; mutations are
  pure API calls (cache left intact - invalidation is the S8 store's targeted refresh).
- presentation/guard/GuardStore.kt - shared StateFlow<Resource<...>> holders; config feed + events
  feed (envelope unwrapped to List<GuardEvent> off the same upstream), the vehicleId>0 gate with a
  stable disabled slot per read, and per-mutation targeted refresh.
- cache/CacheDomain.kt - Guard partition (5s window = the tighter of REALTIME 5s config /
  QUICK 10s events; conservative, never flags fresh what the web considers stale).

Tests (apps/shared/core/commonTest):
- presentation/guard/GuardStoreTest.kt (8 tests) - cache->network for both reads, envelope unwrap,
  the enabled:vehicleId>0 gate (null/blank/0/-1/abc disabled + stable instance), upstream sharing,
  and each mutation routing to the right repo call + the exact feeds the matching web hook
  invalidates (setGuardConfig->config+events, panic->events, acknowledge->events), refresh no-op.
- presentation/guard/GuardGoldenTest.kt (7 tests) - language-neutral golden vectors locking
  isGuardEventAcknowledged, guardVehicleEnabled, guardEventsOf, and the cache-key tuples (KMP+C#
  parity, ADR-004).
- data/repo/GuardRepositoryContractTest.kt (9 tests) - endpoint/method/params/body locks for all
  five calls (GET /vehicles/{id}/guard, GET .../guard/events, POST .../guard with all four body
  keys + explicit null home_geofence_id, POST .../guard/panic, POST
  .../guard/events/{eventID}/acknowledge) and the cache-intact-on-mutation contract.

Note: the prompt's parity table lists useGuardPanic under "reads"; the real web file implements it
as a POST useMutation. The web file is the contract source of truth (per the Single Goal), so it is
ported faithfully as a mutation. All 5 hooks are covered.

=== PARITY ===
Reads (2):
  useGuardConfig            -> GuardRepository.guardConfig            GET  /vehicles/{id}/guard
  useGuardEvents            -> GuardRepository.guardEvents            GET  /vehicles/{id}/guard/events
                                 (select: safeArray(data?.events) -> guardEventsOf)
Mutations (3):
  useSetGuardConfig         -> GuardRepository.setGuardConfig         POST /vehicles/{id}/guard
                                 body {enabled, home_geofence_id, sensitivity, auto_panic}
                                 invalidates config + events
  useGuardPanic             -> GuardRepository.triggerPanic           POST /vehicles/{id}/guard/panic
                                 invalidates events
  useAcknowledgeGuardEvent  -> GuardRepository.acknowledgeGuardEvent  POST /vehicles/{id}/guard/events/{eventID}/acknowledge
                                 invalidates events
Derivations golden-locked (KMP+C#): isGuardEventAcknowledged, guardEventsOf, guardVehicleEnabled,
  guardConfigKey, guardEventsKey.
SI preserved: no unit-bearing fields; values round-trip verbatim, display conversion deferred to S5.
=== END PARITY ===

